    touching the chain.

    Reads and fully validates the segment index and the progress
    cursor and requires them to describe the same prior build:
    equal segment size, frame count and head, a progress index
    fingerprint equal to the index's segment-by-segment
    fingerprint, a boundary that completes a segment, and a last
    complete segment whose trailing digest is the recorded
    boundary digest. Returns ``(progress, complete_fingerprint)``
    when the gate holds -- the fingerprint covering exactly the
    complete segments copied into every continuation -- or
    ``None`` to request the single permitted full rebuild. Any
    cache problem alone never raises.
